div.p:
Beſide this, the Earle of Warwike (as one to whom the common welth was much bounde
                           •…
                        ) was made gouernor of the realme,The Erle of Warwicke inſtituted gouernour of the realme. with whome as fellow was aſſociated George Duke of Clarence. And thus was the ſtate of the realme quite altered. To this Parliament came the Murques Montacute, excuſing himſelfe that for feare of death he declined to take king Edwardes part, which excuſe was accepted.
